                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "NOTHING like the original. As far as I am concerned this game is \"Zoo\" no Tycoon included. Less animals, less creative freedom, less difficulty, less customization. The game itself isnt bad. But it's not Zoo Tycoon. The Zoo Tycoon i grew up with is apparently dust in the wind because this is a copy paste presets game where the only thing you \"customize\" is your barely editable character and where you put exhibit items (IN PRESET LOCATIONS) this game is where creativity goes to wither away. No terrain altering, no paint brushes, no heart. I'd return it (and I've only played for maybe an hour or two max) if it wasn't for the fact that the game itself isnt necessarily bad, it's just that it stripped everything that made zoo tycoon iconic out of it. Should have just named it something else, it's not even close to the original, but in itself isnt a bad game. I'm gonna buy Planet Zoo or Zoo Planet- whatever it's called- next since based on other reviews from both this and that game, everyone in the comments who has played the ACTUAL original Zoo Tycoon can agree that this isnt it, and the other one is much closer to the game we knew and loved. If you like zoo games this isnt bad, pretty cute I guess... but if you wanted Zoo Tycoon? I don't recommend this at all.",
